  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Bea 507.04 Eligible Grant-Funded Activities",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 507.04 Eligible Grant-Funded Activities. HIM grant funds shall be used to support the following new construction or capacity increases of the following types of infrastructure, as long as the improvement supports the program goals of facilitating the development of additional housing in the municipality:\n\n(a) Drinking water infrastructure improvements;\n\n(b) Sanitary sewer infrastructure improvements;\n\n(c) Stormwater system creation, expansion, or upgrades;\n\n(d) Highway infrastructure;\n\n(e) Telecommunications;\n\n(f) Electrical distribution, including switchgear or transformers; and\n\n(g) Fire suppression system upgrades for conversion of existing buildings to residential use in order to meet the requirements of the state fire code and RSA 153:5\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
}
